## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates cost-awareness and decision-making capabilities when designing hybrid ML architectures with latency and privacy constraints—not just model accuracy.

## Key Concepts
- **Hybrid inference economics**: On-device versus edge cost trade-offs with intelligent data routing based on sensitivity, latency, and residency requirements.
- **Data residency and governance**: Regional compliance overhead and architecture implications.
- **Operational robustness**: Rollout strategy, drift detection, fault tolerance, and robust go/no-go criteria for production deployment.

## Code Example
```javascript
function npv(rate, flows) {
  let v = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < flows.length; i++) {
    v += flows[i] / Math.pow(1 + rate, i + 1);
  }
  return v;
}
```

This NPV function calculates net present value to evaluate whether the 18-month investment in the hybrid inference architecture yields positive returns and identifies the break-even horizon.

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design a pragmatic CBA for on-device decision logic that changes user experience while preserving privacy and reducing server load. Tests modeling of energy, storage, and regulatory costs alongside rollout governance.

## Key Concepts

- On-device decisioning and privacy
- Compute and energy modeling
- Data minimization and consent logging
- Telemetry footprint and storage planning
- Rollout gates and break-even analysis

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo cost model for CBA
function cba(params) {
  const energy = params.cpuW * params.hours;
  const storage = params.rulesKB * params.devices / 1024;
  const savings = params.backendCostPerUnit * params.throughputReduction;
  const compliance = params.complianceCost;
  return energy + storage - savings + compliance;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate energy estimates across device SKUs?
- How would you adapt the model for regional regulatory differences?
